    },
    {
     "type": "tip",
     "tag": "Pronunciation",
     "title": "Three sounds for -ed",
     "paras": [
      "After <i>p, k, s, sh, ch, f</i>: a short <b>/t/</b>: <i>stopped, fixed, checked</i>.",
      "After most other sounds: <b>/d/</b>: <i>changed, failed</i>.",
      "After <i>t</i> or <i>d</i>: a new syllable <b>/ɪd/</b>: <i>reported, tested, started</i>. Never add a syllable to <i>stopped</i>: it's one beat, <i>stopt</i>."
     ],
     "list": [
      [
       "stopped, fixed, checked",
       "/t/",
       "m-t"
      ],
      [
       "changed, failed, frozen",
       "/d/",
       "m-d"
      ],
      [
       "reported, tested, started",
       "/ɪd/",
       "m-id"
      ]
     ]
